        self.add_recursive_def(SRC_IR_LZD_DEREF_ACTIVATION, "ir_lzd_deref_activation: *** THE DERIVED DEREF, AS ONE FRAME-GENERIC LEMMA -- FORTY STEPS, NO AUTHORED FUNCTION. *** For every field address holding a NON-NULL Arc pointer below the allocation counter, whose child address BORROWS to itself in the heap the return slot already extended, and for every dests list, underlying frame stack, heap and counter: forty steps of the compiler's own `<LevelArc as Deref>::deref`, `Option::as_deref`, `Option::expect` and `<Arc<Level>>::deref` land on the caller's resumption carrying the child Level's address, with the heap ONE CELL LONGER and the counter ONE HIGHER. ir_lzb_deref_activation is this lemma for an AUTHORED seven-node model, and that model is what this chain exists to retire. \n\nSEVEN rewrites separate the two, and every one of them is a heap operation the emitted code really performs: the Option<Arc> load, as_deref's BORROW of the field address, the Arc load at the SAME cell, Arc::deref's borrow of the CHILD address, the return slot's liveness read, its update, and its read-back. Everything between them the kernel computes. \n\nTHREE PREMISES, each earned rather than assumed. Non-nullness: Option<Arc<Level>> is niche-encoded, so a null word IS None and the run would take expect's panic arm. The counter bound on the field: as_deref allocates, so a field cell at or above the counter would be SHADOWED by the slot. The child's borrow: a borrow is a dereference-time provenance check in this model, so the deref does not merely COMPUTE the child address -- it dereferences it, and the premise is stated at the ALREADY-EXTENDED heap because that is where the dereference happens. `ir_lzd_live_ext` produces exactly that form from the child's own sub-derivation, which is how the relation supplies all three -- and it is why the relation is indexed by a bound and why its children are successors. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.")?;
        self.add_recursive_def(SRC_IR_LZD_MACH0_S, "ir_lzd_mach0_s: one activation of the emitted Level::is_zero body over the DERIVED module, indexed by an IRScalar rather than an address so the induction can recurse on the representation relation. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.")?;
        self.add_recursive_def(SRC_IR_LZD_AFTER_LOAD, "ir_lzd_after_load: the configuration one step in, with the root heap lookup exposed SYNTACTICALLY so a representation hypothesis can rewrite it. The load's type is ir_lzd_tlevel, for which the module's table has NO row -- Level is niche-encoded over five variants and IREnc.nicheptr is two-variant only -- so the view is the identity and the stored aggregate passes through. That refusal is what makes this arm identical to every pre-Phase-B chain's. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.")?;
        self.add_recursive_def(SRC_IR_LZD_STEP_LOAD, "ir_lzd_step_load: the first step rewritten so the root lookup occurs syntactically. Eq.refl -- the content is the SHAPE. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.")?;
        self.add_recursive_def(SRC_IR_LZD_ACTIVATION_ZERO, "ir_lzd_activation_zero: Zero is TRUE in six steps over the DERIVED module -- b0's load, extractfield and switch, b1's const and br, and b6's ret. Six, exactly as over ir_lzb_module, and it must be: a leaf never calls the deref, so no constant on this path moved when the authored model was replaced by four real bodies. The heap and the counter are UNCHANGED, which is also only true of the leaves. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.")?;
