        self.add_recursive_def(SRC_IR_LZD_ACTIVATION_PARAM, "ir_lzd_activation_param: Param is FALSE in six, for every payload, through the emitted body's own b3. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.")?;
        self.add_recursive_def(SRC_IR_LZD_IMAX_SEG, "ir_lzd_imax_seg: IMax over the DERIVED module, reached through the switch DEFAULT edge to b5, which geps to offset 16 ONLY -- the first operand is bound in the cell and NEVER READ, the impredicative collapse, so this arm consumes only the second child's hypothesis. 49 + c2 steps, of which 40 are one activation of the compiler's own four-body deref. NEW against ir_lzb_imax_seg: the heap and the counter MOVE. The deref allocates its return slot, so the run ends at a heap one cell longer than it started and at a counter one higher, and the recursive call runs against THAT heap -- which is why the lemma carries a MemExt witness and re-frames every hypothesis about the entry heap through ir_lzd_lookup_ext. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.")?;
        self.add_recursive_def(SRC_IR_LZD_MAX_FALSE_SEG, "ir_lzd_max_false_seg: Max's SHORT-CIRCUIT edge over the DERIVED module -- the left operand is not zero, so the answer is false and the right operand is NEVER READ. It consumes ih1 and not ih2, and it pays for ONE derived deref rather than two: 54 + c1 steps, where a module that evaluated both operands would take 40 more and still answer false. The heap ends one cell longer than it started plus whatever the left subtree allocated, which is what the MemExt witness carries. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.")?;
        self.add_recursive_def(SRC_IR_LZD_MAX_TRUE_SEG, "ir_lzd_max_true_seg: *** THE DEEPEST MACHINE FACT IN THE CRYSTAL. *** Max's recursive edge with the left operand zero, over the module with NO AUTHORED FUNCTION: four opaque segments -- deref, self, deref, self -- spliced into one 95 + c1 + c2 step activation, of which EIGHTY are two activations of the compiler's own four-body deref. Both children are read and the answer is the SECOND one's. Neither caller frame is ever written out; each callee's stack is named as the tail of the configuration that reaches it. NEW against ir_lzb_max_true_seg, and the reason this lemma is three times the size: the heap MOVES four times -- once per deref, once per subtree -- so every hypothesis about the entry heap is re-framed through ir_lzd_lookup_ext at the state where it is used, and the three extensions are composed into the one the caller is owed. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.")?;
        self.add_recursive_def(SRC_IR_LZD_INIT_MEM, "ir_lzd_init_mem: the heap the machine actually STARTS with -- the caller's heap with one cell materialised per module global, which for this module is the `expect` message at address 0 (a global's id IS its address). It is named because A4's representation premise has to be stated at it and not at the caller's heap: ir_lzb_module carries no global and could keep the two apart, this one cannot, and a Level represented only in a heap the machine never sees would be a premise about nothing. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.")?;
